ed in metagenome mode.", "name": "eggNOG mode select"}], "label": "eggNOG mode select", "name": "Input parameter", "outputs": [], "position": {"left": 3030, "top": 1465}, "tool_id": null, "tool_state": "{\"validators\": [], \"parameter_type\": \"text\", \"optional\": false, \"default\": \"metagenome\", \"multiple\": false, \"restrictions\": [\"proteins\", \"CDS\", \"genome\", \"metagenome\"]}", "tool_version": null, "type": "parameter_input", "uuid": "412a847a-a1a1-482b-9af1-bb1a1b403508", "when": null, "workflow_outputs": []}, "44": {"annotation": "Also predict protein domains and functions with InterProScan. [Functional annotation]", "content_id": null, "errors": null, "id": 44, "input_connections": {}, "inputs": [{"description": "Also predict protein domains and functions with InterProScan.", "name": "Run InterProScan"}], "label": "Run InterProScan", "name": "Input parameter", "outputs": [], "position": {"left": 3030, "top": 1565}, "tool_id": null, "tool_state": "{\"validators\": [], \"parameter_type\": \"boolean\", \"optional\": false, \"default\": true}", "tool_version": null, "type": "parameter_input", "uuid": "7c475ea0-1bdd-4e04-949d-766b14008608", "when": null, "workflow_outputs": []}, "45": {"annotation": "MAGs are nucleotide sequences, so InterProScan runs in DNA/RNA mode. [Functional annotation]", "content_id": null, "errors": null, "id": 45, "input_connections": {}, "inputs": [{"description": "MAGs are nucleotide sequences, so InterProScan runs in DNA/RNA mode.", "name": "InterProScan mode select"}], "label": "InterProScan mode select", "name": "Input parameter", "outputs": [], "position": {"left": 3030, "top": 1665}, "tool_id": null, "tool_state": "{\"validators\": [], \"parameter_type\": \"text\", \"optional\": false, \"default\": \"DNA/RNA\", \"multiple\": false, \"restrictions\": [\"Protein\", \"DNA/RNA\"]}", "tool_version": null, "type": "parameter_input", "uuid": "86421c9b-6ad8-4b0d-99bf-41bc763150c2", "when": null, "workflow_outputs": []}, "100": {"annotation": "Convert the Yes/No long-read selection into a boolean that enables the long-read branch only when requested.", "content_id": null, "errors": null, "id": 100, "input_connections": {"input_param_type|input_param": {"id": 2, "output_name": "output"}}, "inputs": [], "label": "Long-read branch gate", "name": "Long-read branch gate", "outputs": [], "position": {"left": 1320, "top": 465}, "tool_id": "toolshed.g2.bx.psu.edu/repos/iuc/map_param_value/map_param_value/0.2.0", "tool_state": "{\"input_param_type\": {\"type\": \"text\", \"__current_case__\": 0, \"input_param\": {\"__class__\": \"ConnectedValue\"}, \"mappings\": [{\"__index__\": 0, \"from\": \"Yes\", \"to\": \"True\"}, {\"__index__\": 1, \"from\": \"No\", \"to\": \"False\"}]}, \"output_param_type\": \"boolean\", \"unmapped\": {\"on_unmapped\": \"default\", \"__current_case__\": 2, \"default_value\": \"False\"}, \"__page__\": 0, \"__rerun_remap_job_id__\": null}", "tool_version": null, "type": "tool", "uuid": "169154d7-16b5-42d0-8c9c-b3b21316a46a", "when": null, "workflow_outputs": []}, "101": {"type": "subworkflow", "name": "Quality control and trimming of short reads", "label": "Quality control and trimming of short reads", "tool_id": null, "tool_state": "{}", "input_connections": {"Raw reads": {"id": 0, "output_name": "output", "input_subworkflow_step_id": 0}, "Adapter to remove on forward reads": {"id": 3, "output_name": "output", "input_subworkflow_step_id": 1}, "Adapter to remove on reverse reads": {"id": 4, "output_name": "output", "input_subworkflow_step_id": 2}, "Qualified quality score": {"id": 5, "output_name": "output", "input_subworkflow_step_id": 3}, "Minimal read length": {"id": 6, "output_name": "output", "input_subworkflow_step_id": 4}}, "inputs": [], "outputs": [], "annotation": "Embedded workflow: trims adapters and low-quality bases with fastp and summarises read quality with MultiQC.", "when": null, "id": 101, "uuid": "d4750314-8ac8-4dd9-897b-e28da8534f59", "position": {"left": 760, "top": 365}, "workflow_outputs": [{"label": "Trimmed short reads", "output_name": "fastp trimmed reads", "uuid": "b71be1cc-9ece-4fb8-91e1-a01ffaeaf9e3"}, {"label": "Short-read QC report", "output_name": "MultiQC HTML report", "uuid": "458e72b5-a938-41a0-a654-9179d2cd7096"}], "subworkflow": {"a_galaxy_workflow": "true", "annotation": "This workflow performs quality control and trimming on paired-end Illumina fastq(.gz) files using fastp and aggregates the quality control reports with MultiQC", "comments": [], "creator": [{"class": "Person", "identifier": "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9852-1987", "name": "B\u00e9r\u00e9nice Batut"}, {"class": "Person", "identifier": "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2982-388X", "name": "Paul Zierep"}, {"class": "Person", "identifier": "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3602-7884", "name": "Mina Hojat Ansari"}, {"class": "Organization", "name": "FAIRyMAGs consortium", "url": "https://github.com/usegalaxy-eu/FAIRyMAGs"}], "format-version": "0.1", "license": "MIT", "name": "Short-read quality control and trimming", "readme": "# Short-read quality control and trimming\n\nBefore starting any analysis, it is always a good idea to assess the quality of the input data and to discard poor-quality base content by trimming and filtering reads.\n\nThis workflow can be used on its own or integrated into other workflows. For example, it is part of a **suite of workflows for end-to-end metagenome-assembled genome (MAG) generation** (check [FAIRyMAGs repository](https://github.com/usegalaxy-eu/FAIRyMAGs) for the complete workflow suite and its capabilities).\nA dedicated [learning pathway](https://galaxyproject.github.io/training-material/learning-pathways/mags.html) provides detailed guidance on how to use this workflow.\n\nThis workflow takes paired-end Illumina (**short-reads**) fastq(.gz) files and executes the following steps:\n1. Quality control and trimming using **fastp**\n2. Aggregation of the quality control reports using **MultiQC**\n\n## Input Datasets\n\n- A list of paired datasets corresponding to paired-end raw reads in `fastqsanger` or `fastqsanger.gz` format.\n- Qualified quality score: The quality value that a base is qualified to have.\n- Minimal read length: Reads shorter than this value will be discarded.\n- [Optional] Adapter to remove on forward reads and reverse reads\n\n## Output Datasets\n\n- A list of paired datasets corresponding to paired-end **trimmed** reads in `fastqsanger` or `fastqsanger.gz`, ready for further analysis.\n- List of `JSON` reports of fastp for each sample that could be used as inputs for extra MultiQC\n- MultiQC report in HTML\n\n## Funding\n\nThis workflow was developed as part of the [**FAIRyMAGs** project](https://elixir-europe.org/how-we-work/scientific-programme/science/bfsp/fairymags), funded as a commissioned service of the [**Biodiversity, Food Security and Pathogens (BFSP) ELIXIR Scientific Programme 2024\u20132028**](https://elixir-europe.org/how-we-work/scientific-programme/science/bfsp).\n\nThe project was also supported by the **European Galaxy Server**, funded by the German Federal Ministry of Education and Research (BMBF; 031 A538A de.NBI-RBC) and the **Ministry of Science, Research and the Arts Baden-W\u00fcrttemberg (MWK)** within the framework of **LIBIS/de.NBI Freiburg**.", "report": {"markdown": "\n# Workflow Execution Report\n\n## Workflow Inputs\n```galaxy\ninvocation_inputs()\n```\n\n## Workflow Outputs\n```galaxy\ninvocation_outputs()\n```\n\n## Workflow\n```galaxy\nworkflow_display()\n```\n"}, "steps": {"0": {"annotation": "Raw reads as paired-end collection", "content_id": null, "errors": null, "id": 0, "input_connections": {}, "inputs": [{"description": "Raw reads as paired-end collection", "name": "Raw reads"}], "label": "Raw reads", "name": "Input dataset collection", "outputs": [], "position": {"left": 0, "top": 0}, "tool_id": null, "tool_state": "{\"optional\": false, \"tag\": null, \"collection_type\": \"list:paired\", \"fields\": null, \"column_definitions\": null}", "tool_version": null, "type": "data_collection_input", "uuid": "921113d6-60b5-413d-acb5-65b5515a28e2", "when": null, "workflow_outputs": []}, "1": {"annotation": "Sequence of the adapter to remove from forward reads using fastp", "content_id": null, "errors": null, "id": 1, "input_connections": {}, "inputs": [{"description": "Sequence of the adapter to remove from forward reads using fastp", "name": "Adapter to remove on forward reads"}], "label": "Adapter to remove on forward reads", "name": "Input parameter", "outputs": [], "position": {"left": 0, "top": 120}, "tool_id": null, "tool_state": "{\"multiple\": false, \"validators\": [], \"parameter_type\": \"text\", \"optional\": true}", "tool_version": null, "type": "parameter_input", "uuid": "7f4b4c11-a767-46d0-a3e6-5c9fc8667bcb", "when": null, "workflow_outputs": []}, "2": {"annotation": "Sequence of the adapter to remove from reverse reads using fastp", "content_id": null, "errors": null, "id": 2, "input_connections": {}, "inputs": [{"description": "Sequence of the adapter to remove from reverse reads using fastp", "name": "Adapter to remove on reverse reads"}], "label": "Adapter to remove on reverse reads", "name": "Input parameter", "outputs": [], "position": {"left": 0, "top": 260}, "tool_id": null, "tool_state": "{\"multiple\": false, \"validators\": [], \"parameter_type\": \"text\", \"optional\": true}", "tool_version": null, "type": "parameter_input", "uuid": "00addbca-26cf-4aba-ba30-df34414971c1", "when": null, "workflow_outputs": []}, "3": {"annotation": "The quality value that a base is qualified. Default 15 means a quality score &gt;=Q15 is qualified.", "content_id": null, "errors": null, "id": 3, "input_connections": {}, "inputs": [{"description": "The quality value that a base is qualified. Default 15 means a quality score &gt;=Q15 is qualified.", "name": "Qualified quality score"}], "label": "Qualified quality score", "name": "Input parameter", "outputs": [], "position":